# CyberArk AppCode Safe Validator

## Purpose

`Test-AppCodeSafes.ps1` checks whether each account AppCode has CyberArk Safes that start with:

```text
AP-<AppCode>
```

and whether matching Safes end with:

```text
AMNG
OMNG
```

The script is read-only. It does not create, update, or delete anything.

## Input CSV

Default file:

```text
samples/account-appcode-template.csv
```

Required columns:

```csv
AccountID,UserName,Address,AppCode
```

`AppCode` must be exactly 3 letters or numbers.

## Output

Each run creates:

```text
logs/AppCodeSafeValidation_*.log
reports/AppCodeSafeValidation_Report_*.csv
reports/AppCodeSafeValidation_AppCodeSummary_*.csv
```

Main report includes:

```text
AccountID
UserName
Address
AppCode
MatchingAppID
SearchPrefix
HasMatchingAPSafe
HasAMNGSafe
HasOMNGSafe
MatchStatus
AMNGSafes
OMNGSafes
OtherMatchingSafes
AllMatchingSafes
```

## Match Logic

For AppCode `ABC`, the script searches for:

```text
AP-ABC
```

Then it reports:

| Result | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `AMNG_AND_OMNG_FOUND` | Matching AppCode Safes exist for both AMNG and OMNG |
| `AMNG_FOUND_ONLY` | AMNG Safe exists, OMNG was not found |
| `OMNG_FOUND_ONLY` | OMNG Safe exists, AMNG was not found |
| `APPCODE_SAFE_FOUND_NO_AMNG_OR_OMNG` | AppCode Safe exists but does not end in AMNG or OMNG |
| `NO_APPCODE_SAFE_FOUND` | No Safe was found for that AppCode |
| `InvalidAppCode` | AppCode is not exactly 3 letters or numbers |

## Environment Files

`.env`

```ini
TENANT_ID="abq4291"
SUB_DOMAIN="mtbanktest"
PROXY_ADDRESS="proxy.company.com"
PROXY_PORT="8080"
```

`env/dev.env` or `env/prod.env`

```ini
PROXY="http://proxy.company.com:8080"
PVWA="https://mtbanktest.privilegecloud.cyberark.cloud"
```

## Usage

Dev:

```powershell
.\Test-AppCodeSafes.ps1 -Environment dev
```

Prod:

```powershell
.\Test-AppCodeSafes.ps1 -Environment prod
```

Use a different CSV:

```powershell
.\Test-AppCodeSafes.ps1 -CsvFile .\samples\account-appcode-template.csv -Environment prod
```

Use proxy credentials:

```powershell
.\Test-AppCodeSafes.ps1 -Environment prod -ProxyUseDefaultCredentials
```

## Notes

- The script uses the same env/proxy/auth style as the account field updater.
- It prompts for CyberArk Identity service-user credentials.
- The bearer token is kept only in memory.
- Only a short SHA256 token fingerprint is logged.
- Duplicate AppCodes are cached so CyberArk is searched once per unique AppCode.
- Do not commit real `.env`, `dev.env`, `prod.env`, logs, reports, or production CSV data to Git.
